--TEST--
a `??` whose default is a bare `$m + 10` offers two groupings, the parentheses that keep what the line does and the `??` applied first, `rule:expressions/misread-grouping-warns`, `rule:ide/a-quick-fix-is-a-diagnostics-own-suggestion`
--FILE--
<?nvs
?int $n = 5;
int $m = 0;
echo $n ?? $<|>m + 10;
--REQUEST--
codeAction
--EXPECT--
4:6-4:19 quickfix apply `??` first: `($n ?? $m) + 10` -> "($n ?? $m) + 10"
4:8-4:12 refactor.rewrite Put on separate lines -> "\n    ?? "
4:12-4:19 quickfix keep the current meaning: `$n ?? ($m + 10)` -> "($m + 10)"
